G1024.def:
βραχύς, -εῖα, -ύ, 
[in LXX chiefly for מְעַט ;] 
short; 
__(a) of time; short, little: βραχύ, Actes 5:34; μετὰ β., Luc 22:58; β. τι, a short time, Hébreux 2:7, 9 RV, mg.; 
__(b) of distance: Actes 27:28; 
__(with) of quantity or value, little, few: Jean 6:7, Hébreux 2:7, 9 RV, txt.; pl., διὰ βραχέων, in few words, Hébreux 13:22.
†

G1067.def:
γέεννα (γέενα, Marc 9:45, Rec.), -ης, ἡ (perh. through Aram. גֵּיהִנָּם, from Heb. גֵּי הִנֹּם, Néhémie 11:30; גֵּי בֶּן־הִנֹּם, Jean 18:16; גֵּי בּנֵי־הִנֹּם, 4Ki.23:10; valley of (the son, sons of) lamentation); 
[in LXX the nearest approach to γ. is γαίεννα, Josué 18:16 (Γαὶ Ὀννόμ, A), elsewhere φάραγξ Ὀνόμ (Josué 15:8, al.), V. Swete on Marc 9:43 ;] 
Gehenna, a valley W. and S. of Jerusalem, which as the site of fire-worship from the time of Ahaz, was desecrated by Josiah and became a dumping-place for the offal of the city. Later, the name was used as a symbol of the place of future punishment, as in NT: Matthieu 5:29, ; 10:28, Marc 9:43, 45 47, Luc 12:5, Jacques 3:6; γ. τ. πυρός, Matthieu 5:22 18:19, prob. with ref. to fires of Moloch (DB, ii, 119b); υἱὸς γεέννης, Matthieu 23:15; κρίσις γεέννης, 23:33.†

G1074.def:
γενεά, -ᾶς, ἡ 
(γίγνομαι), [in LXX chiefly for דּוֹר, דֹּר (Cremer, 148) ;] 
__1. race, stock, family (in NT, γέννημα, which see). 
__2. generation; 
__(a) of the contemporary members of a family: pl., Matthieu 1:17 (cf. Genèse 31:3, מוֹלֶדֶת); metaphorically, of those alike in character, in bad sense, Matthieu 17:17, Marc 9:19, Luc 9:41 16:8, Actes 2:40; 
__(b) of all the people of a given period: Matthieu 24:34, Marc 13:30, Luc 21:32, Philippiens 2:15; pl., Luc 1:48; esp. of the Jewish people, Matthieu 11:16 12:39, 41 42, 45 16:4 23:36, Marc 8:12, 38 Luc 7:31 11:29, 30-32, 50, 51 17:25, Actes 13:36, Hébreux 3:10" (LXX) ; τὴν γ. αὐτοῦ τίς διηγήσεται, Actes 8:33 (LXX); 
__(with) the period covered by the life-time of a generation, used loosely in pl. of successive ages: Actes 14:16 15:21, Éphésiens 3:5, Colossiens 1:26; εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ. (= לִדוֹר וָדוֹר, al.), Luc 34:17, al), Luc 1:50; εἰς πάσας τὰς γ. τοῦ αἰῶνος τῶν αἰώνων, Éphésiens 3:21 (Ellic, in l.; DCG, i, 639f.).
†

G1093G.def:
γῆ, γῆς, ἡ, 
[in LXX for אֲדָמָה ,אֶרֶץ, etc. ;] 
__1. the earth, world: Luc 21:35, Actes 1:8, Hébreux 11:13, Apocalypse 3:10, al.; opposite to οὐρανός, Matthieu 5:18 11:25, Marc 13:27, al. 
__2. land; 
__(a) opposite to sea or water: Marc 4:1, Luc 5:3, Jean 6:21, al.; 
__(b) as subject to cultivation: Matthieu 13:5, Marc 4:8, Luc 13:7, Hébreux 6:7, al.; 
__(with) the ground: Matthieu 10:29, Marc 8:6, Luc 24:5, Jean 8:6, al.; 
__(d) a region, country: Luc 4:25, Romains 9:28, Jacques 5:17; γῆ Ἰσραήλ, Matthieu 2:20, 21; Χαλδαίων, Actes 7:4; ἡ Ἰουδαία γῆ, Jean 3:22; with genitive of person(s), Actes 7:3.

